// Fixture: §3 4575 silent-accept check probe.
//
// `reify check` exits 0 and prints "All constraints satisfied." even though
// the range argument "not-a-range" is a String literal, not a Range<Angle>.
// The compiler performs NO nominal arg-vs-param rejection for this concrete
// param (the 4575-class bug): the mistyped argument is silently accepted.
//
// The mistyped argument sits at the range: the axis is a checked Direction
// slot since direction-typing ζ-a (#9640), so a mistyped axis is rejected and
// would no longer probe silent acceptance.
//
// Used as the negative-assertion / FAIL probe in the committed probe set:
//   expected = {observation: "present", match: {exit_code: 1}}
//   (we expect a rejection diagnostic, observed=absent → FAIL)

structure def RevoluteSilentAccept {
    let j = revolute(dir(0, 0, 1), "not-a-range", point3(0mm,0mm,0mm))
}
